-- ============================================================================
-- H1 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Safety Performance Statistics & KPIs, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/safetystats/advanced.
--
-- What this tier owns: WHETHER ANYTHING IS CHANGING. The u-chart with varying
-- exposure: exposure units, a pooled centre line and limits that move with
-- each period's hours; a signal lies strictly outside its limits and the
-- lower limit is floored at zero and flagged; what a signal means, and
-- revising the limits after a found cause the intervention did not produce;
-- before and after an intervention, with and without the flagged month;
-- benchmarking against the IOGP published figures on the same base and the
-- same definition; the traps in denominators, contractors and
-- reclassification; and judgement end to end. Digest sections 21 to 27, and
-- section 28.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The centre line is pooled, so every limit is
-- drawn from the whole series, and a before-and-after comparison can turn on
-- one flagged month. The Expert capstone grades the centre, two limits, a
-- revised centre and the two before-and-after p-values that disagree for a
-- reason.
-- ============================================================================

values ('safetystats', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-u-chart","title":"The u-Chart","lesson_keys":["l01-exposure-units-on-the-chosen-base","l02-the-centre-line-is-pooled","l03-limits-that-move-with-exposure","l04-the-lower-limit-floored-at-zero","l05-two-charts-the-engine-will-not-draw"]},{"key":"m02-signals","title":"Signals","lesson_keys":["l01-strictly-outside-its-limits","l02-three-sigma-and-what-a-band-costs","l03-a-low-point-that-signals","l04-small-exposure-and-wide-limits"]},{"key":"m03-what-a-signal-means","title":"What a Signal Means","lesson_keys":["l01-a-signal-asks-a-question","l02-revising-the-limits-after-a-found-cause","l03-no-signal-is-a-weak-reassurance","l04-before-and-after-an-intervention"]},{"key":"m04-benchmarking","title":"Benchmarking","lesson_keys":["l01-reading-the-iogp-published-rates","l02-same-base-and-same-definition-first","l03-a-benchmark-is-a-population-figure","l04-the-five-year-view"]},{"key":"m05-the-traps","title":"The Traps","lesson_keys":["l01-denominators-that-move","l02-contractor-events-and-contractor-hours","l03-reclassification","l04-rate-chasing","l05-the-mean-of-rates-one-level-up"]},{"key":"m06-judgement-end-to-end","title":"Judgement, End to End","lesson_keys":["l01-a-year-on-one-chart","l02-what-the-engine-does-not-classify","l03-writing-the-monitoring-note","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
